    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="report-header">
            <h1>UK Retail Fuel Price Trend Analysis</h1>
            <div class="subtitle">A comprehensive analysis of retail fuel pricing patterns across UK forecourts, examining price distributions by fuel type and temporal update behaviour based on government-mandated open data.</div>
            <div class="meta">
                <strong>Analysis Period:</strong> {date_min.strftime('%Y-%m-%d')} to {date_max.strftime('%Y-%m-%d')} | 
                <strong>Generated:</strong> {datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%d')} | 
                <strong>Audience:</strong> Government Policy Analysts & Energy Economists
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="kpi-grid">
            <div class="kpi-card">
                <div class="kpi-label">Unique Stations</div>
                <div class="kpi-value">{total_stations:,}</div>
                <div class="kpi-sub">Forecourts in dataset</div>
            </div>
            <div class="kpi-card">
                <div class="kpi-label">Total Records</div>
                <div class="kpi-value">{len(df_clean):,}</div>
                <div class="kpi-sub">After data cleaning</div>
            </div>
            <div class="kpi-card">
                <div class="kpi-label">Median Update Lag</div>
                <div class="kpi-value">{lag_median:.2f}h</div>
                <div class="kpi-sub">Source to recorded</div>
            </div>
            <div class="kpi-card warning">
                <div class="kpi-label">Records with Lag &gt; 24h</div>
                <div class="kpi-value">{lag_over_24h:,}</div>
                <div class="kpi-sub">({lag_over_24h/len(df_clean)*100:.1f}% of dataset)</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="section">
            <h2>1. Dataset Overview & Coverage Summary</h2>
            <p>This analysis is based on official UK government fuel price reporting data collected from the Fuel Finder API, aggregated by fuelcosts.co.uk. The dataset provides retail fuel prices at individual forecourt level across England, Scotland, and Wales.</p>

            <table>
                <tr><th>Metric</th><th>Value</th></tr>
                <tr><td>Total Price Records</td><td>{len(df_clean):,}</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Unique Forecourts (node_id)</td><td>{total_stations:,}</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Fuel Types</td><td>6 (E10, E5, B7_STANDARD, B7_PREMIUM, B10, HVO)</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Analysis Period</td><td>{date_min.strftime('%Y-%m-%d')} to {date_max.strftime('%Y-%m-%d')}</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Invalid Price Records Removed</td><td>{len(df) - len(df_clean):,} (prices &lt;50 or &gt;500 pence)</td></tr>
            </table>

            <h3>Data Quality Notes</h3>
            <p>120 records were removed as price outliers (77 with prices below 50p, 43 with prices above 500p — outside the range of legitimate UK fuel prices). The remaining {len(df_clean):,} records form the basis of this analysis.</p>
