                <img src="data:image/png;base64,{chart2}" alt="Price Spread Analysis">
                <div class="chart-caption">Figure 3: IQR and Max-Min spread comparison by fuel type — higher values indicate greater price variability across stations</div>
            </div>

            <h3>Key Observations</h3>
            <p><strong>E10 shows the lowest price spread</strong> (185.89p range) with the tightest IQR (16p), indicating a more standardised market. In contrast, <strong>E5 and HVO show the highest spreads</strong> (324.40p and 383.00p respectively), suggesting consumers face meaningful price disparities for premium fuels. Standard diesel (B7_STANDARD) also shows substantial variation with a 233.90p spread.</p>
        </div>

